{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000205",
  "title": "Fourier Series",
  "created_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "shared_cargo_toml": "[profile.release]\nopt-level = 1\nlto = false\ncodegen-units = 16",
  "description": "Visualize how sine harmonics build up square, sawtooth, and triangle waves with animated epicycles.",
  "tags": [
    "mathematics",
    "fourier",
    "animation",
    "simulation",
    "signal-processing"
  ],
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "cell_intro",
      "order": 0,
      "label": "Introduction",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "# Fourier Series \u2014 Epicycle Visualization \ud83c\udfa1\n\nAny **periodic function** can be decomposed into a sum of sine and cosine harmonics \u2014 this is the Fourier series:\n\n$$f(x) = \\frac{a_0}{2} + \\sum_{n=1}^{N} \\left[ a_n \\cos(nx) + b_n \\sin(nx) \\right]$$\n\nFor **purely odd functions** (only sine terms), three classic waveforms emerge from their Fourier coefficients:\n\n| Waveform | Series |\n|---|---|\n| **Square** | $\\displaystyle\\frac{4}{\\pi}\\sum_{n=1,3,5,\\ldots}^{N}\\frac{\\sin(nx)}{n}$ |\n| **Sawtooth** | $\\displaystyle\\frac{2}{\\pi}\\sum_{n=1}^{N}\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}\\sin(nx)}{n}$ |\n| **Triangle** | $\\displaystyle\\frac{8}{\\pi^2}\\sum_{n=1,3,5,\\ldots}^{N}\\frac{(-1)^{(n-1)/2}\\sin(nx)}{n^2}$ |\n\n## How the Visualization Works\n\n- **Left panel**: Rotating circles (_epicycles_), one per harmonic. Each circle's radius equals the harmonic's amplitude scaled to pixels; it rotates at the harmonic's angular frequency $n$.\n- **Right panel**: The y-coordinate of the outermost tip is recorded each frame, tracing the waveform over time (newest on the left, scrolling right).\n- **Dashed line**: Connects the epicycle tip to the current waveform entry point.\n- **Dotted overlay**: The ideal target waveform for reference.\n\nAs you increase the number of harmonics the approximation sharpens \u2014 watch the **Gibbs phenomenon** overshoot appear at the sharp corners of the square and sawtooth waves!"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_controls",
      "order": 1,
      "label": "Controls",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "(\n    ui::slider(\"terms\", 1.0, 25.0)\n        .step(1.0)\n        .label(\"Number of Harmonics\")\n        .default_value(5.0),\n    ui::dropdown(&[\"Square\", \"Sawtooth\", \"Triangle\"])\n        .name(\"waveform\")\n        .label(\"Waveform\")\n        .default_value(\"Square\"),\n)"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_vis",
      "order": 2,
      "label": "Fourier Visualization",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "use std::f64::consts::PI;\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Constants \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\nconst W: u32 = 800;\nconst H: u32 = 400;\nconst EPI_CX: f64 = 195.0;\nconst EPI_CY: f64 = 200.0;\nconst SCALE: f64 = 80.0;       // pixels per unit amplitude\nconst MAX_HIST: usize = 360;   // rolling wave history length (pixels)\nconst WAVE_X: u32 = 415;       // left edge of waveform panel\nconst WAVE_W: u32 = 375;       // width of waveform panel\nconst DT: f64 = 0.025;         // time step per frame (radians)\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Spectral palette (one colour per harmonic) \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\nfn harmonic_color(idx: usize) -> (u8, u8, u8) {\n    const P: [(u8, u8, u8); 8] = [\n        (255,  80,  80),\n        (255, 160,  40),\n        (240, 220,  40),\n        ( 80, 220,  80),\n        ( 40, 200, 255),\n        (100, 100, 255),\n        (180,  80, 255),\n        (255,  80, 200),\n    ];\n    P[idx % 8]\n}\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Ideal waveforms (amplitude \u00b11, phase-matched to the Fourier series) \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n//\n// All three series start at 0 when t = 0 (all sin terms vanish), so each\n// ideal function is also 0 at t = 0.\n\nfn ideal(t: f64, kind: u32) -> f64 {\n    match kind {\n        0 => t.sin().signum(),\n        1 => {\n            // t/\u03c0 on (\u2212\u03c0, \u03c0) with period 2\u03c0; shifted so that f(0) = 0.\n            let t_pos = ((t + PI) % (2.0 * PI) + 2.0 * PI) % (2.0 * PI);\n            (t_pos - PI) / PI\n        }\n        _ => (2.0 / PI) * t.sin().asin(),\n    }\n}\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Drawing helpers \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\nfn in_bounds(x: i32, y: i32) -> bool {\n    x >= 0 && x < W as i32 && y >= 0 && y < H as i32\n}\n\nfn draw_line(c: &mut Canvas, x0: i32, y0: i32, x1: i32, y1: i32, col: (u8, u8, u8)) {\n    let dx = (x1 - x0).abs();\n    let dy = -(y1 - y0).abs();\n    let sx: i32 = if x0 < x1 { 1 } else { -1 };\n    let sy: i32 = if y0 < y1 { 1 } else { -1 };\n    let mut err = dx + dy;\n    let (mut x, mut y) = (x0, y0);\n    loop {\n        if in_bounds(x, y) {\n            c.set_pixel(x as u32, y as u32, col);\n        }\n        if x == x1 && y == y1 { break; }\n        let e2 = 2 * err;\n        if e2 >= dy { err += dy; x += sx; }\n        if e2 <= dx { err += dx; y += sy; }\n    }\n}\n\nfn draw_ring(c: &mut Canvas, cx: f64, cy: f64, r: f64, col: (u8, u8, u8)) {\n    if r < 1.0 { return; }\n    let steps = ((2.0 * PI * r) as usize + 32).max(48);\n    for i in 0..steps {\n        let a = 2.0 * PI * i as f64 / steps as f64;\n        let px = (cx + r * a.cos()) as i32;\n        let py = (cy + r * a.sin()) as i32;\n        // keep rings inside the epicycle panel\n        if in_bounds(px, py) && px < WAVE_X as i32 {\n            c.set_pixel(px as u32, py as u32, col);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nfn draw_dot(c: &mut Canvas, cx: i32, cy: i32, r: i32, col: (u8, u8, u8)) {\n    for dy in -r..=r {\n        for dx in -r..=r {\n            if dx * dx + dy * dy <= r * r && in_bounds(cx + dx, cy + dy) {\n                c.set_pixel((cx + dx) as u32, (cy + dy) as u32, col);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Simulation state \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\nstruct FourierVis {\n    time: f64,\n    // y-deviation of the tip from EPI_CY each frame (screen coords, + = down).\n    // history[0] = oldest, history[last] = newest.\n    history: Vec<f64>,\n}\n\nimpl Simulation for FourierVis {\n    fn init() -> Self {\n        Self { time: 0.0, history: Vec::with_capacity(MAX_HIST + 1) }\n    }\n\n    fn tick(&mut self) -> Canvas {\n        let terms = sim::read::<f64>(\"terms\").unwrap_or(5.0).clamp(1.0, 25.0) as u32;\n        let kind  = sim::read::<f64>(\"waveform\").unwrap_or(0.0) as u32 % 3;\n\n        self.time += DT;\n\n        // Build harmonic list: (frequency n, amplitude, phase offset).\n        // Positive amplitude; phase \u03c0 flips the sine via sin(nt + \u03c0) = \u2212sin(nt).\n        let harmonics: Vec<(u32, f64, f64)> = match kind {\n            0 => (0..terms).map(|k| {\n                let n = 2 * k + 1;\n                (n, 4.0 / (n as f64 * PI), 0.0)\n            }).collect(),\n            1 => (1..=terms).map(|n| {\n                let ph = if n % 2 == 0 { PI } else { 0.0 };\n                (n, 2.0 / (n as f64 * PI), ph)\n            }).collect(),\n            _ => (0..terms).map(|k| {\n                let n = 2 * k + 1;\n                let ph = if k % 2 == 1 { PI } else { 0.0 };\n                (n, 8.0 / (n as f64 * n as f64 * PI * PI), ph)\n            }).collect(),\n        };\n\n        // Trace the epicycle chain to find each joint position.\n        let mut ex = EPI_CX;\n        let mut ey = EPI_CY;\n        let mut pts: Vec<(f64, f64)> = vec![(ex, ey)];\n        for &(n, amp, ph) in &harmonics {\n            let r = amp * SCALE;\n            let a = n as f64 * self.time + ph;\n            ex += r * a.cos();\n            ey += r * a.sin();\n            pts.push((ex, ey));\n        }\n\n        // Record y-deviation: screen y of tip minus center.\n        // Wave is plotted as  py = EPI_CY + dev  which equals ey \u2014 same screen\n        // y as the tip, making the connecting line perfectly horizontal.\n        let dev = ey - EPI_CY;\n        self.history.push(dev);\n        if self.history.len() > MAX_HIST {\n            self.history.remove(0);\n        }\n\n        // \u2500\u2500 Render \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n        let mut c = Canvas::new(W, H);\n        c.fill((8, 8, 20));\n\n        // Horizontal axis (both panels)\n        for px in 0..W {\n            c.set_pixel(px, EPI_CY as u32, (22, 22, 42));\n        }\n        // Vertical axis (epicycle panel)\n        for py in 0..H {\n            c.set_pixel(EPI_CX as u32, py, (22, 22, 42));\n        }\n        // Panel divider\n        for py in 0..H {\n            c.set_pixel(409, py, (35, 35, 60));\n            c.set_pixel(410, py, (35, 35, 60));\n        }\n\n        // \u2500\u2500 Epicycles \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n        for (i, w) in pts.windows(2).enumerate() {\n            let (x0, y0) = w[0];\n            let (x1, y1) = w[1];\n            let (_, amp, _) = harmonics[i];\n            let r = amp * SCALE;\n            let col = harmonic_color(i);\n            // Dim ring outline\n            let dim = (col.0 / 5, col.1 / 5, col.2 / 5 + 8);\n            draw_ring(&mut c, x0, y0, r, dim);\n            // Radius arm in full colour\n            draw_line(&mut c, x0 as i32, y0 as i32, x1 as i32, y1 as i32, col);\n        }\n\n        // Bright dot at the tip\n        let &(tip_x, tip_y) = pts.last().unwrap_or(&(EPI_CX, EPI_CY));\n        draw_dot(&mut c, tip_x as i32, tip_y as i32, 3, (255, 255, 255));\n\n        // \u2500\u2500 Waveform panel \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n        // Ideal waveform: dotted overlay (pixel offset i = newest \u2026 oldest)\n        for off in 0..WAVE_W {\n            let t_at = self.time - off as f64 * DT;\n            let iv = ideal(t_at, kind);\n            // iv \u2208 [\u22121, 1] where +1 means below centre (screen convention)\n            let py = (EPI_CY + iv * SCALE) as i32;\n            let px = WAVE_X + off;\n            if (off / 5) % 2 == 0 && px < W && py >= 0 && py < H as i32 {\n                c.set_pixel(px, py as u32, (50, 50, 90));\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Traced wave history: newest at WAVE_X, older scrolling right\n        let n_hist = self.history.len();\n        for (i, &val) in self.history.iter().rev().enumerate() {\n            let px = WAVE_X + i as u32;\n            if px >= W { break; }\n            // py = EPI_CY + val = ey (same screen y as the tip when recorded)\n            let py = (EPI_CY + val) as i32;\n            if py < 0 || py >= H as i32 { continue; }\n            let brightness = 1.0 - i as f64 / n_hist as f64;\n            let r = (30.0 + 225.0 * brightness) as u8;\n            let g = (80.0 + 120.0 * brightness) as u8;\n            let b = (180.0 +  70.0 * brightness) as u8;\n            c.set_pixel(px, py as u32, (r, g, b));\n            if py + 1 < H as i32 {\n                c.set_pixel(px, (py + 1) as u32, (r / 3, g / 3, b / 3));\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Dashed connecting line: epicycle tip \u2192 waveform panel entry\n        let conn_y = tip_y as i32;\n        for px in (tip_x as i32)..WAVE_X as i32 {\n            if (px / 4) % 2 == 0 && conn_y >= 0 && conn_y < H as i32 {\n                c.set_pixel(px as u32, conn_y as u32, (90, 90, 155));\n            }\n        }\n        // Small dot at the entry point\n        draw_dot(&mut c, WAVE_X as i32, conn_y, 2, (220, 220, 255));\n\n        c\n    }\n\n    fn fps() -> u32 { 30 }\n}"
    }
  ]
}
